{
  "preset": "WFM stereo (FM broadcast)",
  "description": "FM broadcast in stereo: the Analyzer channel on the station, ~200 kHz wide (demodulator OFF lets it be that wide). MPX at 192 kS/s: L+R below 15 kHz, pilot 19 kHz, L-R on 38 kHz. The pilot PLL built from blocks (a feedback loop through a Delay): MPX -> x * conj(v) -> Im (phase error) -> PID (PI: wn = 2 pi 5 rad/s, zeta 0.7 for a 7.5 kHz pilot) -> + 19 kHz -> FM modulator (the VCO) -> z^-16 -> back. Locked, v lags the pilot by 90 deg, so the 38 kHz subcarrier sin(2 p) = -Im(v^2) (the multiplier's \"Times\" -1). The probe shows the VCO's offset from 19 kHz.",
